cervix to 8 mm was measured objectively and the cervical diameter before surgical dilatation was recorded. RESULTS      
Following isosorbide mononitrate or gemeprost, a lower cumulative force was required to dilate the cervix to 8 mm and a 
higher cervical diameter before dilatation was recorded. Pretreatment with glyceryl trinitrate reduced the cumulative   
force required to dilate the cervix but had no effect on cervical diameter. CONCLUSIONS Like the prostaglandin analogue 
gemeprost, the nitric oxide donors isosorbide mononitrate and glyceryl trinitrate can effect cervical ripening. Nitric  
oxide donors may provide an alternative to prostaglandins for cervical ripening before surgical procedures in the first 
trimester."                                                                                                             
